ty 2. Provide the full layer structure. 3. Combine the keys and values of both sections into one continuous text block. 4. State the maximum amount the entire layer covers. 5. Identify the percentage share of the reinsurer. 6. Calculate the exact monetary amount the reinsurer is liable for in a total loss scenario. "Deductible": 1. Identify the base deductible 2.List deductibles for specific risks like Windstorm, Flood, Earthquake, and Testing. 3. Check if there is any clauses that defines how deductibles are applied to consecutive natural disasters. "Terms_and_Conditions": 1. Terms and Conditions 2. Identify all clauses and items starting from the "Terms and Conditions" or "Clauses" section. 3. Combine all identified clauses into one single text response. 4. Ensure each specific clause or numbered item starts on a new line (using a line break/carriage return). 5. Do not summarize, paraphrase, or omit any clause. Keep the original numbering and the full technical wording. "Extension_Clauses": 1. identify all "Extension Clauses" that broaden the scope of the standard policy wording to assess the full breadth of risk. 2. Combine all identified clauses into one single text response. 3. Ensure each specific clause or numbered item starts on a new line (using a line break/carriage return). 4. Do not summarize, paraphrase, or omit any clause. Keep the original numbering and the full technical wording. "Additional_Information": 1. Capture all "Supplementary Data" and "Contextual Notes" that are not part of the standard financial or period fields but are crucial for contract management. 2. Note any technical details about the project (e.g., testing phases, specific materials). 3. Identify the contact persons or departments listed for the Reinsured and Reinsurer. 4. List any comments or notes found in the footer or the very last page that don't fit into standard categories. "ProportionalReinsurance": Identify the sharing ratios and financial distribution in a Proportional Reinsurance treaty. [ "CurrencyVal" : Convert any currency symbols or names into their official ISO 4217 three-letter codes. "GrossPremium" : Gross Premium "Reins" : Reinsurance Share (e.g,. not 19% but 19) "ReComm" : Reinsurance Commission (e.g,. not 19% but 19) "NetReInsPremium" : Net Reinsurance Premium (e.g,. not 19% but 19) ] }

