n. 3. Combine all identified clauses into one single text response. 4. Ensure each specific clause or numbered item starts on a new line (using a line break/carriage return). 5. Do not summarize, paraphrase, or omit any clause. Keep the original numbering and the full technical wording. "Extension_Clauses": 1. identify all "Extension Clauses" that broaden the scope of the standard policy wording to assess the full breadth of risk. 2. Combine all identified clauses into one single text response. 3. Ensure each specific clause or numbered item starts on a new line (using a line break/carriage return). 4. Do not summarize, paraphrase, or omit any clause. Keep the original numbering and the full technical wording. "Additional_Information": 1. Capture all "Supplementary Data" and "Contextual Notes" that are not part of the standard financial or period fields but are crucial for contract management. 2. Note any technical details about the project (e.g., testing phases, specific materials). 3. Identify the contact persons or departments listed for the Reinsured and Reinsurer. 4. List any comments or notes found in the footer or the very last page that don't fit into standard categories. "ProportionalReinsurance": Identify the sharing ratios and financial distribution in a Proportional Reinsurance treaty. [ "CurrencyVal" : Convert any currency symbols or names into their official ISO 4217 three-letter codes. "GrossPremium" : - Gross Premium - Number without comma and without non-numerical values "Reins" : Reinsurance Share (e.g,. not 19% but 19) "ReComm" : Reinsurance Commission (e.g,. not 19% but 19) "NetReInsPremium" : Net Reinsurance Premium (e.g,. not 19% but 19) ] "Total_Sum_Insured": 1. The value of Total Sum Insured can be found on several sections. 2. Total Sum Insured for asset values and 'Limit of Liability' for coverage caps or liability sections. 3. Perform a mathematical summation of all identified amounts to calculate all numeric values for the Total Sum Insured "Total_Sum_Insured_Currency": 1. Convert any currency symbols or names into their official ISO 4217 three-letter codes. "TSIbyLocation" : (1) It should be same as Total_Sum_Insured [ "TSI": 1. It should be same as Total_Sum_Insured "TSI_Currency": 1. Total Sum Insured Currency for the section. 2. Convert any currency symbols or names into their official ISO 4217 three-letter codes. ] "LocationbyTSI" : Physical location for the Location by TSI [ "Location" : The detail address for the location ] }
